    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="1107" n="957" xml:id="pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2618/4–5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bryan to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-01-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 279.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your cable
                    message of this date as follows,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d326-f1"/> and to state
                    that the Diario do Governo of the 24th instant published the text of the said
                    agreement, a copy of which I transmit herewith.</p>
                <p>In reply to your No. 113 of January 11, 1907, File No. 2618/2, I have the honor
                    to state that on the 8th of January the King of Portugal ratified the agreement
                    extending to Porto Rico the provisions of the commercial agreement between the
                    United States and Portugal, as reported in my dispatch No. 277 of January
                    22.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
